<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bernhard II of Lippe</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1140–1224</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bernhard II was lord of Lippe in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/westphalia">Westphalia</a> and a companion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-the-lion">Henry the Lion</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duke-of-saxony">Duke of Saxony</a>. Around 1185 he founded the town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lippstadt">Lippstadt</a>, and he also founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lemgo">Lemgo</a>, laying the foundations of the later principality of Lippe. In later life he became a monk and went to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livonia">Livonia</a>, where he served as abbot of Dünamünde and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> of Selonia during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livonian-crusade">Livonian Crusade</a>.</p></div>
